## Boundary

Agreement across all conjugate roots of one rational prime is stronger than a
single-root calculation, but it is not a characteristic-zero upper proof. A
minor can vanish in every factor modulo one prime without vanishing over the
number field. G3DH therefore does not claim
`rank_Q(gamma)(Q)=4748`.

The common 4,748-column basis and 1,274-column defect now provide the canonical
target for a second fraction-free factorization. Promotion needs either exact
`Q(gamma)` relations for those 1,274 columns, a characteristic-zero certified
factorization through 4,748 coordinates, or enough independent good primes
plus a proved height bound.

No H02 values, source contraction, path solution, integral marking, readout or
`beta_C` decision is inferred.

